# perf-diagnosis — performance gate (mobile)

> Any task touching performance must produce **measurements** before fixes. The `perf_gate.py` hook surfaces this rule whenever a prompt contains a perf trigger word (`慢 / 卡 / 延迟 / 优化 / jank / lag / slow / perf`).

## Gate

> **Do NOT write a perf fix without numbers.**

The sequence is:

1. **Reproduce** the symptom locally; record the steps
2. **Measure** with the stack's profiler (commands below)
3. **Hypothesise** the root cause from the measurements (not from intuition)
4. **Fix** addressing the measured cause
5. **Re-measure** to verify the fix moved the metric in the right direction
6. **Handoff** includes before/after numbers + raw profile output paths

Any task-md without measurements in `§起草前 baseline 实证` and `§ 时序约束 / 性能数据` is a hint that this gate was skipped.

## Per-stack profilers

### Android

| Tool | Use case |
|---|---|
| Android Studio Profiler | CPU / memory / energy / network in dev workflow |
| `dumpsys gfxinfo {package}` | Frame timing histogram (jank rate) |
| Perfetto (`perfetto -c config.pbtx`) | Cross-process traces, kernel-level scheduler view |
| Systrace (legacy) | If team still on it |
| `adb bugreport` | Full system snapshot when issue is system-wide |
| LeakCanary | Memory leak detection in debug builds |

Key numbers to capture: frame time P50/P95/P99, jank rate (% slow frames), main-thread CPU spike duration, memory delta.

### iOS

| Tool | Use case |
|---|---|
| Instruments.app | CPU / allocations / time profiler / leaks |
| `xcrun xctrace record --template "Time Profiler"` | Headless trace capture for CI |
| Console.app | Real-device log stream with predicate filters |
| MetricKit (`MXMetricPayload`) | Field-collected metrics from real users (if instrumented) |
| Charles / mitmproxy | Network capture with bandwidth shaping |

Key numbers: main-thread CPU%, hang duration (per MXHangDiagnosticPayload spec), launch time (cold/warm/resume).

### Flutter

| Tool | Use case |
|---|---|
| Flutter DevTools (browser) | CPU / memory / widget tree / network |
| `flutter run --profile` | Frame timing breakdown in DevTools |
| Observatory / Dart VM Service | Dart-level allocation tracking |
| `flutter doctor -v` | Environment-related slowness |
| Underlying platform profilers (adb / Instruments) | When the issue is below Flutter |

Key numbers: build time per frame, layout time, paint time, raster time.

### Harmony

| Tool | Use case |
|---|---|
| DevEco Studio Profiler | CPU / memory / energy |
| `hdc shell hidumper` | System service / hap state dump |
| SmartPerf-Host | Cross-process performance trace (similar to Perfetto) |
| `hdc shell hilog` | Runtime log stream with bundle filter |
| `hdc bugreport` | Full system snapshot |

Key numbers: frame time, FPS, JS thread CPU, GPU rendering pipeline timing.

## §perf-gate trigger words

The hook fires on (default list, overridable in `.sulde-config.yaml: enforcement.perf_gate.triggers`):

`慢 / 卡 / 卡顿 / 延迟 / 优化 / 提速 / 加载慢 / 进场慢 / 响应慢 / jank / lag / perf / performance / slow`

When the hook fires, you see a reminder. The reminder is **not blocking** — the dev's responsibility is to honour the gate manually.

## How a perf task-md looks

A coordinator drafting a perf task-md must include:

```markdown
## §起草前 baseline 实证

### Step 1: 近 14 天 commit
- (relevant frontend) commits possibly affecting this hot path

### Step 5: scaffold 数值 vs design-truth cross verify
- N/A for perf (or note design-truth motion-timing constraint)

## §诊断数据 (mandatory for perf task-md)

### Repro steps
1. ...
2. ...

### Baseline measurements (before fix)
- jank rate: 8.2% (50 trials, dumpsys gfxinfo)
- main-thread spike P95: 120ms (Android Studio Profiler)
- raw trace: `.ai-workspace/diag/{date}-{task}-baseline.perfetto-trace`

### Hypothesised cause
The measurements suggest X is doing Y on main thread during onAppear...

### Target after fix
- jank rate < 1%
- spike P95 < 50ms
```

## What this gate prevents

Without numbers, devs (and coordinators) tend to add "defensive" delays / debounces / coroutine dispatchers / `runOnUiThread` calls that don't address the actual cost. The fix appears to work locally because it shifts the spike off the screen the dev is looking at — then re-emerges elsewhere.

See `<docs-hub>/ADR/0003-mobile-cold-flow-stateflow.md` for one form this takes (cold Flow used where StateFlow is needed).
